{"timestamp": 1783631265.119091, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I reported Diana\u2019s body in security.\n\nMy route was weapons -> security -> navigation -> back to security. In weapons, Alice entered from security around tick 4. Then I went to security and saw Diana enter from electrical around tick 6; she was alive in security through ticks 7 and 8. Frank entered security from weapons at tick 8 while Diana was still there. I then went toward navigation, and I saw Frank enter navigation from security around tick 12 and stay there briefly. When I came back to security, Diana was dead there.\n\nSo the main thing I can say is: Diana was alive in security when Frank came in, and later I found her dead in that same room. Not hard accusing yet, but Frank was the only person I personally saw near her after she was alive."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631279.068467, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I get why that looks bad from Eve\u2019s POV, but I didn\u2019t kill Diana.\n\nMy route was oxygen -> upper engine -> medbay -> cafeteria -> weapons -> security -> navigation. I came into security from weapons, saw Diana there alive, and I left pretty quickly toward navigation. Eve saw me in navigation around tick 12, so I was not still sitting in security. Then I saw Eve leave navigation back toward security at tick 13.\n\nSo from my side: Diana was alive when I passed through, I went to navigation, Eve was with/near me there, then Eve went back and reported. That could be a normal report, but it also means Eve was the one who doubled back to the body location after I left.\n\nI\u2019d like to hear where Alice/Bob/Charlie were, especially if anyone came through electrical or weapons/security after me. Right now this feels like either Eve is assuming based on proximity, or it\u2019s a possible self-report."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631297.968321, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I can confirm the early part of Eve\u2019s route matches mine somewhat: I started in security, went to weapons, then continued cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper engine. I did not go back to security after leaving.\n\nI didn\u2019t see Diana at all this round, and I didn\u2019t see the body. I also didn\u2019t personally encounter anyone on my route, so I can\u2019t vouch for Bob or Charlie yet.\n\nFrom what\u2019s been said, I don\u2019t think I\u2019m a good suspect because I left security before Diana was seen alive there by Eve. The key window sounds like after Diana was alive in security around ticks 7-8. Frank was definitely there with her, then later went to navigation. That doesn\u2019t clear him because the kill could\u2019ve happened before he left for nav, but Eve also doubled back and reported, so self-report isn\u2019t impossible.\n\nI want to hear Bob and Charlie\u2019s routes before deciding, especially if either of them passed through electrical, weapons, or security after Diana went in."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631313.321004, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Bob here. My route was lower_engine -> storage -> medbay -> cafeteria -> weapons. I didn\u2019t encounter anyone at all, and I never went into security, so I didn\u2019t see Diana or the body.\n\nFrom the info so far, Alice sounds less likely to me because Eve says Diana was alive in security after Alice had already left that area. The main window seems to be after Diana was seen alive in security around ticks 7-8.\n\nFrank being seen in navigation later doesn\u2019t fully clear him, because if he was in security with Diana first, the kill could\u2019ve happened before he left. Eve self-report is possible since she doubled back and found it, but her route has been pretty detailed and partly corroborated.\n\nI really need Charlie\u2019s route before voting, especially whether Charlie went through electrical/security/weapons. If Charlie wasn\u2019t near security, I\u2019m leaning Frank more than Eve right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631328.336374, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I was medbay -> upper_engine -> lower_engine, and I didn\u2019t see anyone at all. I never went to security, weapons, or electrical, so I didn\u2019t see Diana or the body.\n\nOne small note: Frank says he went through upper_engine and medbay early, but I didn\u2019t see him there. That\u2019s not a hard contradiction because timing/vision could explain it, but I can\u2019t confirm that part of his route.\n\nBased on everyone\u2019s info, Alice and Bob both sound away from the kill area, and I was away too. So this really comes down to Eve versus Frank. Eve\u2019s report is detailed and Alice confirms the early weapons/security timing. Frank was the only person clearly placed in security with Diana after she was alive, and being seen in navigation later doesn\u2019t clear him if the kill happened before he left.\n\nSelf-report is possible, but I think the stronger evidence is on Frank. I\u2019m leaning vote Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631347.533654, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Given everyone\u2019s routes, I think this is pretty narrowed down.\n\nAlice left security before Diana was even seen alive there by me. Bob says he never went security, and his route was away. Charlie also says he never went security/weapons/electrical and was away. No one has placed either Bob or Charlie near the body.\n\nFor the actual window: Diana entered security from electrical at tick 6, I saw her alive at ticks 7 and 8, then Frank entered security from weapons at tick 8 while Diana was still there. I left toward navigation, and then I saw Frank come into navigation from security at tick 12. When I went back to security, Diana was dead.\n\nSo unless someone is lying about being nowhere near security, Frank is the only one confirmed in the room with Diana during the kill window. I understand he\u2019s pushing self-report, but from my perspective I found the body after leaving him coming from that direction. I\u2019m voting Frank unless someone has a stronger contradiction."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631366.2151098, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I\u2019m going to push back because this is getting treated like I was caught on top of the body, and that\u2019s not what happened.\n\nI saw Diana alive in security when I passed through. I did not stay there \u2014 I went to navigation, and Eve herself confirms she saw me in navigation at tick 12. Then I saw Eve leave navigation back toward security at tick 13, and she\u2019s the one who reports the body there.\n\nSo the confirmed sequence from my POV is: Diana alive in security, I pass through, I\u2019m seen away from the room, then Eve goes back to the body location and reports. That is absolutely a possible self-report window.\n\nAlso, everyone else\u2019s routes are basically self-reported. I\u2019m not hard accusing Bob or Charlie, but nobody actually has proof they were away except their own word. The only hard info is Eve and me around security/nav, and I know I didn\u2019t kill Diana.\n\nEve\u2019s story is detailed, yes, but reporters always have detailed body info. The detail doesn\u2019t clear her. I think voting me here is too easy based on proximity, when Eve is the last confirmed person heading back to security right before the report. My vote is almost certainly Eve unless someone has something new."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631382.195735, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I\u2019m still on the same page here: I started security -> weapons -> cafeteria -> oxygen -> upper_engine, and I never went back to security after leaving. Eve seeing me in weapons early lines up with that, and Diana was apparently alive in security after I had already left, so I don\u2019t think I fit the window.\n\nFor the actual kill, I think it\u2019s mainly Eve versus Frank. I understand Frank\u2019s point that Eve went back and reported, so self-report is possible. But the strongest confirmed fact is still that Frank was in security with Diana after she was alive, and then Diana ends up dead there. Being seen in navigation later doesn\u2019t clear him if the kill happened before he left.\n\nBob and Charlie both claim away from security, and nobody has contradicted that. So unless we think one of them is completely lying about route and slipped into security unseen, the most likely option to me is Frank. I\u2019m leaning Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631394.277745, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "My info hasn\u2019t changed: I was lower_engine -> storage -> medbay -> cafeteria -> weapons, and I didn\u2019t see anyone the whole route. I never went into security, electrical, or navigation, so I can\u2019t give direct body info.\n\nBut from the stories, I think this is still narrowed to Eve vs Frank. I agree self-report is possible in theory, but the timeline makes Frank look worse to me:\n\n- Diana is confirmed alive in security by Eve.\n- Frank is confirmed entering security while Diana is alive.\n- Frank later comes from security into navigation.\n- Then Eve goes back and reports Diana dead in security.\n\nIf Frank killed before leaving security, then him being in navigation later doesn\u2019t clear him at all. Eve could be self-reporting, but I don\u2019t see why she would give such a specific timeline that puts Frank there unless she\u2019s taking a big gamble.\n\nAlice seems cleared from timing because Diana was alive after Alice left. Charlie and I are both claiming routes away, and nobody has contradicted us. So between Eve and Frank, I\u2019m leaning Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1783631403.3944058, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 15, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My info is still the same: I was medbay -> upper_engine -> lower_engine, didn\u2019t see anyone, and I never went near security, weapons, electrical, or navigation. So I can\u2019t directly confirm the body or who was in the room.\n\nLooking at everyone\u2019s stories, I think Alice is pretty unlikely because she left security before Diana was confirmed alive there. Bob and I are both claiming routes away from security, and nobody has contradicted either of us.\n\nThat leaves Eve and Frank. I agree self-report is possible, but the stronger confirmed timeline is that Frank entered security while Diana was alive, then later came out from security toward navigation, and Diana was found dead in security after that. Being seen in navigation later doesn\u2019t clear him if the kill happened before he left.\n\nSo unless Eve is making a risky self-report, Frank had the clearest opportunity. I\u2019m voting Frank."}}
